    "The exact cold request and finite answer match across reported suites. Decode outputs match by trial across all four common J/V repetitions; 4090 decode outputs differ and its MTP maximum is 3 rather than 2. These are bounded smoke workloads, not comprehensive quality qualification.",
    "Whole-phase vmstat includes startup/model-load/lifecycle activity. Benchmark-window counters are periodic host-wide observations, not precise per-process accounting, and may miss subsecond boundary activity.",
    "The two V benchmark windows show pswpout delta 0, while phase one has host pswpout 5044. Zero cgroup swap is not proof that the host never paged.",
    "J and V differ in driver, CPU, RAM, desktop GPU activity and physical upstream PCIe width (J x4, V x16). Even a matched-model cross-card result cannot isolate unlock causality.",
    "UTC boot-unlock anchors are V 2026-10-25T13:11:45.282904+00:00 and 4090 2026-10-26T02:18:08.390111+00:00. Classify historical samples individually; no same-card same-driver locked/unlocked A/B or causal unlock percentage is available.",
    "Do not compare historical throughput at unlike prompt lengths or label samples after unlock as pre-unlock baselines.",
    "Dense probe numerical references passed, but the operator failed clock plausibility. Preserve raw values without a qualified clock-normalized, Tensor Core, unlock or LLM-speedup claim.",
    "J normal desktop GPU load was 31% before its run (Code SM samples 16-19%, Brave 12-15%); applications were left running. The common-model comparison measures the deployed hosts under these conditions.",
    "J host major-fault deltas in the observed benchmark windows were 24930 and 6065, while its benchmark child cgroups recorded only 4 and 0 major faults across the entire phases. Host fault activity cannot be attributed to the child and indicates substantial background/platform activity.",
    "Common-model V exceeds J by 19.9015% native prefill and 17.6039% native decode in these runs. This is a measured deployed cross-host difference, not a causal GPU-unlock percentage."
